  "coordinate_convention": "Rows of basis_B are the scaled Euclidean coordinates of the catalogue basis. For the public ambient Gram G, B*B^T = 96*G. An integer row z represents z*B/sqrt(96) in the lattice; if z*G*z^T = 6, its unit vector is z*B/24.",
